      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** doses, with the frequency adjusted to the intended daily total.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
